---
title: "Topics · LOD-AM"
description: "The LOD-AM topics: a small controlled vocabulary for the field, linked to Wikidata."
permalink: /topics/
---
{%- macro tree(list) %}
<ul class="topic-tree">
  {%- for t in list %}
  {%- set n = collections.blog | postsWithTopic(t.name) | length %}
  <li><a href="{{ t.path }}">{{ t.label }}</a>{% if n %} <span class="text-body-secondary small">({{ n }})</span>{% endif %}
    {%- if t.narrowerTopics.length %}{{ tree(t.narrowerTopics) }}{% endif %}</li>
  {%- endfor %}
</ul>
{%- endmacro %}
<div class="reading-column ms-0">
  <h1 class="mb-3">Topics</h1>
  <p class="lead">Posts on this site are filed under a small controlled vocabulary for the field LOD-AM works in. Each topic is linked to <a href="https://www.wikidata.org/">Wikidata</a>.</p>
  {{ tree(topicVocab.top) }}
  <p class="small text-body-secondary mt-4">Vocabulary: <a href="https://github.com/LOD-AM/knowledge-graph/blob/main/data/vocab/topics.ttl">topics.ttl</a> (SKOS) in the LOD-AM knowledge graph. The number in brackets is the number of posts.</p>
</div>
